ren who  loved him  and you know the tragedy of the  brillante virtuoso is that he was killed  before he had a chance to do that  iliopolis did actually uh do okay  financially out of this believe it or  not uh one of the things that happened  was that the bank which had loaned the  money to illiopolis to buy the burlante  virtuoso wrote off the debt in the  course of this litigation concluding  that it would never be recovered so from  the debt side he was free and clear by  destroying the vessel with a fire he was  able to you know Escape debts of in the  region of 60 70 million dollars and the  ship was losing losing enormous amount  of money and was coming towards the end  of its life so from a from a purely  Financial point of view destroying the  burlante virtuos so it was the best  thing he could have done  part of me is expected people in the  shipping world to come out and say  it's not that bad you know it's not as  bad as this one ship makes it appear to  be but no one's done that and you know  unfortunately I think there is this  underbelly to to global Shipping that is  thriving and there seems to be very  little that anyone can do about it the  more you dig the worse it seems to look
 

